# Components: compound + context

When a domain entity has multiple related UI parts (e.g. movie → title, rating, poster, genres), do **not** flat-export standalone components that each take slices of the data as props.

Use a **compound component** with Svelte context: one `Root` owns the data; children read it via `useX`.

## Structure

```
components/movie/
  context.svelte.ts   # createMovie / useMovie
  movie-root.svelte   # accepts {movie}, calls createMovie
  movie-title.svelte  # calls useMovie(), renders title
  …
  index.ts            # namespace exports (Root, Title, …)
```

## Context API

Always name the pair `createX` (set) and `useX` (get):

```ts
// context.svelte.ts
import { createContext } from 'svelte';
import type { Movie } from '#lib/…';

export const [useMovie, createMovie] = createContext<Movie>();
```

- `createMovie({ get id() { … }, … })` — call only in `Root`; pass **getters** (see `context-create-getters` rule), not a plain snapshot
- `useMovie()` — call in every child part; do not accept the entity (or its fields) as props when context already provides them

## Namespace exports

```ts
// index.ts — ✅ GOOD
export { default as Root } from './movie-root.svelte';
export { default as Title } from './movie-title.svelte';
export { default as Rating } from './movie-rating.svelte';
// …
```

```ts
// ❌ BAD — prefixed flat exports + prop drilling
export { default as MovieTitle } from './movie-title.svelte';
export { default as MovieRating } from './movie-rating.svelte';
```

## Consumer usage

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import * as Movie from '#lib/components/movie/index.js';
</script>

<Movie.Root {movie}>
	<Movie.Title />
	<Movie.Rating />
	<Movie.Poster />
</Movie.Root>
```

`Root` passes `{movie}` into context; parts like `<Movie.Title />` read from `useMovie()` — no `title={movie.title}` prop drilling.

## Do not

- Export `MovieTitle`, `MovieRating`, etc. as the public API when they belong to one entity
- Pass entity fields into child parts when those parts sit under `Root`
- Use ad-hoc `setContext`/`getContext` string keys — use `createContext` + `createX`/`useX`
- Mix namespace parts with a parallel flat “pass everything as props” API for the same entity
